<title>USA: P-Com jumps on TELCEL pact.</title>
<headline>P-Com jumps on TELCEL pact.</headline>
<dateline>CAMPBELL, Calif. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of P-COM Inc rose about 15 percent after it said it signed an agreement valued at $4 million to supply digital microwave radios to TELCEL, a unit of Telefonos de Mexico.</p>
<p>P-COM rose 4-1/8 to 31-5/8.</p>
<p>Although the total deal is valued at about $4 million, P-COM said it has received an initial purchase order for $800,000.</p>
<p>P-COM said its radios will be used in TELCEL's 1997 expansion plan. TELCEL has captured more than 50 percent of all Mexican cellular subscribers in Mexico, P-COM said.</p>
<p>P-COM develops, manufactures and markets millimeter-wave radio systems for the worldwide wireless telecommunications market.</p>
<p>(( New York newsdesk 212-859-1610 ))</p>
